## the rule set behind --config auto, as the registry serves it
bytes=2423491
rules named=1073  (the policy offers these; semgrep filters to the languages present)
sha256=d246b00122958b0ca9ce20dd927c7c33396db80ec070b00754f6218718297b4d

## why the resolved policy is not vendored as the pin
gitleaks over a vendored copy of the policy file:
  private-key (rule, not value)
  slack-webhook-url (rule, not value)
  — the registry's own example credentials inside its rule metadata, so pinning by vendoring
    would need the secret scan to skip that file, which the audit will not do.

